    "post": "\"Hire fast, fire faster\" is terrible advice.\n\nMost leaders should ignore it.\n\nBecause 99.99% of companies aren't OpenAI or Anthropic.\n\n↳ You don't have their buzz.\n↳ You don't have their brand.\n↳ You don't have their budget.\n\nSo you'll never win playing their game.\n\nHere's your actual reality:\n\n↳ You can't afford \"been there, done that\" resumes.\n↳ You can't wait months for the flawless hire.\n↳ You can't out-pay the giants.\n\nThat's why the CEO quote above lands so hard.\n\n\"Invest heavily in the people you have and you won't waste money buying the people you need.\"\n\nThe math backs it up.\n\nReplacing someone costs 1.5 to 2x their salary.\nDeveloping someone costs a fraction of that.\n\nBut here's what most leaders miss.\n \nThis only works if you're great at three things:\n\n1. Spotting mispriced talent\n↳ See what others overlook.\n↳ Hire for potential, not polish.\n↳ Bet on character and coachability.\n\n2. Offering what others can't\n↳ Steep growth curves, not empty promises.\n↳ Real opportunity, personal and financial.\n↳ Meaningful work, not ping-pong tables.\n\n3. Developing people on purpose\n↳ Honest feedback, not platitudes.\n↳ Regular coaching, not annual reviews.\n↳ Stretch assignments, not generic training.\n\nSo skip \"hire fast, fire faster.\"\n\nHire intentionally.\nDevelop deliberately.\nEmpower enthusiastically.\n\nYour best investment was never overpaying for the mythical perfect hire.\n\nIt's making everyone so good you can afford to lose anyone.\n\n♻️ Repost to inspire more leaders to invest in their people.\n\nFollow Dave Kline for more leadership insights.\n\nP.S. Want proven management playbooks? \nGet them free: mgmtplaybook.com",
