    "post": "Your best person decided to leave months before they resigned.\n\nAnd nobody, including you as their leader, noticed.\n\nA leader I know lost the strongest person on his team last year.\n\nShe never complained.\nShe never missed a deadline.\nShe never asked for anything.\n\nIn her exit conversation, she said one thing that struck a nerve in him:\n\"I never knew where I was going here.\"\n\nHe was stunned.\n\nNothing dramatic had happened.\nNo argument, no bad review, no big moment.\n\nJust small habits that felt fine, because she never pushed back.\n\nHigh performers rarely announce they're unhappy.\nThey keep delivering, go quiet, and start looking.\n\nHere are 8 habits that lose them:\n\n❌ Never ask where they want to go next\n❌ Reward reliability with more work\n❌ Talk about their career once a year\n❌ Assume quiet means fine\n❌ Keep their wins inside your team\n❌ Wait for them to ask for the promotion\n❌ Let the brilliant jerk slide because they deliver\n❌ Say a quick \"good job\" and move on\n\nAnd here are 8 that keep them:\n\n✅ Ask about their next step every quarter\n✅ Reward reliability with a bigger challenge\n✅ Talk about their growth in every one-on-one\n✅ Check in on the quiet ones first\n✅ Put their work in front of senior leaders\n✅ Open the door before they have to ask\n✅ Protect them from the people who drain them\n✅ Name exactly what they did and why it mattered\n\nWhen your strongest person leaves, the rest of the team is watching.\nEveryone learns what growth looks like here, or that there isn't any.\n\nNone of these habits is hard to start.\n\nThe cost comes from waiting until the resignation letter.\n\nWhen did you last ask your best person where they want to go next?\n\nIf your leaders need help building habits like these, I can bring them to your team and tailor them to where you're at right now.\n\nFind out more about working with me here: https://lnkd.in/gGJEEJ5N\n\n♻️ Repost for a leader who needs to check in on their best person.\nFollow me, Cicely Simpson, for more on keeping the people who make your team work.",
