    "post": "Some of my best friends couldn't care less about my ad spend.\n\nThat's exactly why I keep them close.\n\nWhen I think about what makes a life wealthy, relationships are part of it, right alongside money.\n\nAnd the relationships worth holding onto are the people who want to see you win.\n\nI don't have hundreds of founders on speed dial.\nI have a handful who are on journeys a lot like mine.\n\nWhen things get rough, any of us can pick up the phone and say, “I'd really like your opinion on this,” and get the other person's full attention.\n\nThen there are the friends who have nothing to do with business. \n\nThey make me laugh, and they remind me who I am outside of what I do.\n\nAnd of course, there's my family.\n\nMy husband and my darling boys remind me why I'm on this path in the first place.\n\nWe support each other where we can, and make plenty of memories along the way.\n\nGrowing your network has its place.\n\nBut the people who've been with you from the start are the ones who'll keep showing up.\n\nTag someone you're proud to have in your corner!\n\nP.S. For more posts on building a wealthy life, follow Lise Kuecker.\n\nAnd if y'all want to read more on what six business exits taught me,\nsign up for my weekly newsletter, Growth Factor: bit.ly/Growth_Factor",
