    "height": 900,
    "post": "Every founder needs a YouTube team.\n\nI built one in Claude that packages, edits and clips every video, and I'm giving it away for free 👇\n\nIt runs your channel the way a good producer does. It packages the video before anyone edits it, then cuts it and takes your notes on the timeline. Then it picks which moments deserve a second life as shorts.\n\nHere's how it works:\n\n1/ You give it the raw recording\n2/ It writes the titles and thumbnail ideas first, in a few versions to test\n3/ It edits the full video, and you put your taste into the first 30 seconds\n4/ You leave notes at the exact second, and it fixes them\n\nWhat's inside:\n\n➤ Leveling Up Content Engine, the skill that turns 1 recording into the edit and the clips\n➤ Packaging YouTube Thumbnails, the skill that writes the titles and builds the thumbnail tests\n➤ A review board where you leave notes on the timeline, like comments on a doc\n➤ A check that decides which moments are worth a short or a post on X and LinkedIn\n\nSince we started running it, our click-through rate went from about 4% to 6-8% a video, and 30-second retention from about 50-55% to 62-65%.\n\nI'm giving away free access below 👇\n\nP.S. If you're recording videos and nobody on your team has time to package them, this is exactly what you need.",
