    "post": "𝗞𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗦𝗮𝘂𝗱’𝘀 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝗿𝘁𝘂𝗽 𝗠𝗮𝗳𝗶𝗮\n\n12 alumni founders. Over $350 million in reported startup funding.\n\nKing Saud University’s entrepreneurial network is helping shape Saudi Arabia’s growing startup ecosystem.\n\nHere are 3 key takeaways:\n\n1️⃣ Fintech is attracting significant capital\nFounders behind Rewaa, neoleap, Salasa, and Sifi are building businesses across payments, financial services, and commerce infrastructure.\n\n2️⃣ Innovation extends across industries\nFrom Intelmatix and its AI solutions to logistics, real estate technology, and digital platforms, alumni are tackling diverse market opportunities.\n\n3️⃣ University networks can create powerful ecosystems\nShared educational backgrounds can help entrepreneurs build relationships, exchange expertise, and access valuable business connections.\n\nBottom line?\n\nSome of the strongest startup ecosystems are built around networks of ambitious founders.\n\nWhen talent, capital, and entrepreneurial experience come together, the potential for innovation multiplies.\n\n🔔 P.S. Raising capital?\n\nFind the right investors for your startup in 30 seconds.\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/ehddabZ5",
